This repository contains agent skills, reference documentation, golden test
fixtures, and CI tooling for analyzing and porting prebid-server bidder
adapters across language implementations.

The skills describe and ground patterns observed in:
  - prebid/prebid-server (https://github.com/prebid/prebid-server) — Apache License 2.0
  - prebid/prebid-server-java (https://github.com/prebid/prebid-server-java) — Apache License 2.0

The Adapter Specification format and the shared canonical references
(adapter-spec.md, behavior-taxonomy.md, port-translation-rules.md) describe
upstream behavior; they are derivative analytical works.

Golden specifications under prebid-server-{go,java}/read/test-fixtures/ copy
the bytes of upstream `static/bidder-params/{bidder}.json` files verbatim into
the `bidder_params_json` field for SHA-256 byte-fidelity verification. Those
bytes remain under Apache License 2.0 from upstream.

PR numbers, reviewer GitHub handles, file paths, and behavioral observations
quoted in this repository are taken from public upstream sources.
